            <ArticleTitle>Localized eosinophilic gastroenteritis with necrotizing granulomas presenting as acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>510-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eosinophilic gastroenteritis is a condition of unknown aetiology that has been frequently reported involving the stomach and bowel. The colon is rarely cited as a site for the condition. We report a patient suffering from allergic symptoms (asthma, atopic dermatitis, elevated serum IgE levels) who presented with colonic perforation due to eosinophilic colitis with necrotizing granulomas.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
